---
export const prerender = true

import DefaultLayout from '@layouts/DefaultLayout.astro'
import PageHeader from '@components/PageHeader.astro'
---

<DefaultLayout
  title="About — Bishal Upadhyaya"
  description="Applied AI engineer. Neuroscience and medical imaging first, then model efficiency, then products people use. Independent — consulting, pilots and research collaborations."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title="Research on one end, systems people use on the other."
    subtitle="I started by recording electrical signals in living neural circuits. The habits carried over."
  />

  <section class="ab">
    <div class="ab-inner">
      <figure class="ab-portrait" data-reveal="settle">
        <img
          src="/about-portrait.webp"
          alt="Bishal Upadhyaya"
          width="880"
          height="586"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </figure>

      <p class="ab-lead" data-reveal>
        I work independently with founders and research teams: a conversation or a small proof first, then a
        focused pilot, then whatever the work turns out to need. What I am good at is getting to the real shape
        of a hard problem quickly, building something convincing enough to argue with, and then making that
        thing survive contact with production.
      </p>

      <section class="ab-block" data-reveal>
        <h2>What I build</h2>
        <ul class="ab-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Systems that understand signals.</strong> Audio, video, speech, and the messy human data that
            behaves like none of them. Representation learning, temporal alignment, retrieval that has to be both
            cheap and right, and evaluation honest enough that the numbers survive a second look.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Agents and LLM systems that survive production.</strong> Tool calling with structured outputs,
            multi-model routing, evals in the loop, honest failure reporting. Every demo on this site runs on this,
            and says so out loud when the upstream is down.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Models small enough to run where they have to.</strong> Distillation and structured pruning
            without giving up recall. The <a href="/notes/choon">fingerprinting model</a> does its work at a size
            most teams reach for a much larger network to match.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="ab-block" data-reveal>
        <h2>How the work has moved</h2>
        <p>
          It began in a lab, on <em>C. elegans</em>: which innexin proteins build the electrical synapses behind
          an avoidance behaviour, and later whether an engineered synapse could route information around a neuron
          that had been destroyed. Then medical imaging — comparing PET biomarkers for predicting Alzheimer's,
          with attention to which of them a person without access to the expensive scan could actually get. Then
          model efficiency, with collaborators at NVIDIA and Thermo Fisher: how to find the smaller network
          hiding inside the large one.
        </p>
        <p>
          That last paper is not a citation on this site. It is
          <a href="/#work">running inside a product</a>, identifying audio at catalog scale on a single CPU core.
          Music is where these systems ship today. The problems underneath them are not musical.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="ab-block" data-reveal>
        <h2>Where it is going</h2>
        <p>
          The thread I keep pulling on is measurement of the difficult kind: attention, behaviour, well-being,
          the texture of someone's actual experience. Those are the things most worth getting right and the
          easiest to fake progress on. I would rather build instruments for them slowly and honestly than
          quickly and not.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="ab-cta" data-reveal>
        <a class="btn-pill" href="/#contact">Send me something</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</DefaultLayout>

<style lang="scss">
  .ab {
    padding: var(--space-2xl) 0 var(--space-3xl);
  }

  /* Same container as the page header and every home-page band, so the column
     starts on the same left edge rather than floating in a centred well of its
     own. The measure is set on the children instead. */
  .ab-inner {
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 var(--space-l);
    max-width: 1200px;
  }

  .ab-inner > * {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .ab-portrait {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xl);
    max-width: 520px;

    img {
      display: block;
      box-shadow: var(--lift-1);
      border: 1px solid var(--hairline-on-ink);
      border-radius: 14px;
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
    }
  }

  .ab-lead {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2xl);
    color: var(--paper);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .ab-block {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);

    h2 {
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-m);
      color: var(--paper);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    }

    p {
      margin: 0 0 var(--space-m);
      color: var(--paper-soft);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.8;

      &:last-child {
        margin-bottom: 0;
      }
    }
  }

  .ab-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;

    li {
      border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline-on-ink);
      padding: var(--space-m) 0;
      color: var(--paper-soft);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.8;

      &:last-child {
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline-on-ink);
      }

      strong {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
        color: var(--paper);
        font-weight: 600;
      }
    }
  }

  .ab-cta {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 479px) {
    .ab-inner {
      padding-inline: var(--space-m);
    }
  }
</style>
